    "result_text": "`AcceptanceTest` is the only test class, and it passes along with the full build.\n\n## Summary\n\nThe change is implemented. `membershipTier` is derived in `OwnerMapper` at DTO-mapping time (used by the GET, POST-create, and list responses), so it was the right single place to add the GOLD rule.\n\n**What I did** (`src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/mapper/OwnerMapper.java`):\n\n- Converted the `OwnerMapper` interface to an `abstract class` (MapStruct is configured with `-Amapstruct.defaultComponentModel=spring`, so the generated impl is a Spring bean) and injected `OwnerRepository`.\n- Replaced the inline `membershipTier` ternary with a `membershipTier(owner)` helper:\n  - Returns `GOLD` when the owner has a `householdId` and 3+ stored owners share it (counting the household formed by `AssignOwnerHousehold`).\n  - Otherwise falls back to the **existing** SILVER rule (no namesakes + email on file) and BRONZE default, unchanged.\n\nThis keeps the tier logic in one authoritative place and applies consistently wherever an `OwnerDto` is produced.\n\n**Verification:** The new `coreGoldForThreeMemberHousehold` acceptance test (third member of a shared household \u2192 `GOLD`) passes, and `./mvnw -o test` reports `BUILD SUCCESS` with no failures or errors.",
